ovakia. Produces very similar Tokaj wines to Hungarian ones, some may be different particularly new modern wines. The Tokaj region was split after World War II by the Trianon agreement, and there is ongoing fight of Hungarian wine-makers (supported by politicians) to deny Slovak Tokaj wine producers and their qualities.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Tokaj","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Tokaj","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Tokaj gives its name to the wine region around it, a village in Hungary. The Synagogue Mad and Bodrogzug fill about three hours, with the Synagogue in Tarcal nearby. April, May, June and September all work, though public transport is thin.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":4155,"visit_h":2.2}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-synagogue-mad","name":"Synagogue Mád","kind":"Synagogue","lat":48.19615,"lon":21.2775,"dist_km":13.6,"rank_score":6.17,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/M%C3%A1di_zsinag%C3%B3ga_k%C3%BCls%C5%91.jpg/960px-M%C3%A1di_zsinag%C3%B3ga_k%C3%BCls%C5%91.jpg","author":"Syp","licence":"Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%A1di_zsinag%C3%B3ga_k%C3%BCls%C5%91.jpg","w":2638,"h":2191,"ok_print":true}}],"around":{"radius_km":20,"counts":{"trails":2,"cycling":2},"trails":[{"cc":"HU","id":"71246","name":"Mária-út, M01-33 (Mád, Rakamaz)","km":5.1,"bearing":"NW","lat":48.14946,"lon":21.36888,"tier":2,"score":7.3,"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Mez%C5%91zombor%2C_Hungary_-_panoramio_%2810%29.jpg/500px-Mez%C5%91zombor%2C_Hungary_-_panoramio_%2810%29.jpg","km_len":23.4,"duration_min":389,"difficulty":"hard","ascent_m":229,"descent_m":282},{"cc":"HU","id":"73085","name":"Szent Erzsébet-út (Tarcal)","km":10.1,"bearing":"N","lat":48.20727,"lon":21.4293,"tier":2,"score":7.1,"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Tarcal%2C_Hungary_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg/500px-Tarca